# Developmental Algorithms Have Meaning!

**Authors:** Green, John

## Abstract
Adapts Stanic and McKillip's ideas for the use of developmental algorithms to propose that the present emphasis on symbolic manipulation should be tempered with an emphasis on the conceptual understanding of the mathematics underlying the algorithm. Uses examples from the areas of numeric computation, algebraic manipulation, and equation solving to illustrate this proposition. (ASK)

**Source:** https://eric.ed.gov/?id=EJ600143

